yes I do. We are one of a few companies worldwide that are part of the
Teamlinks CAB each year. We get all the Teamlinks EFTs. We've heard
that numerous times. I called in a problem with Teamlinks over Decnet
to an ALl-in-1 server. The support person couldn't replicate the
problem cause they were using Exchange servers over TCP/IP. The
TEAMLINKS support person is using Exchange.

Our backbone is DECnet and even Digital isn't using it. 

It's all so sad. We are looking at so many DEC products that are in
their "twilight years" that we rely on. We expect our network
protocol, message client, messaging server, message transport, server
operating system, remote LAN access, and networking OS all to change
now that Compaq has acquired DEC. At least before there was some hope,
but now, we can't imagine things going anywhere but further south
fast. Since we migrated to Dell PCs from Compaq over two years ago
(with no regrets whatsoever) I imagine the only business we'll end up
doing with Compaq is buying Alphas.





