I guess I hadn't looked close enough or far back enough. Sure enough, I've
got assorted digital logo stuff back to about 1970, with a pretty complete
rainbow of colors. Whatever the background of the manual was, the letters
are that color, and the background boxes are a contrasting color.

I guess the blue to red change was on business cards in the early 90s. All
the cards I ever saw during my 12 years at Digital, from 1980-1991 had blue
chicklets.



