On Thu, 25 Jun 1998 21:44:39 -0400, "Larry Stefani" <noone@anywhere.com>
wrote:

>
>Richard Dervan wrote in message <35917332.8326458@news2.abraxis.com>...
>>
>>On another note, the system has a Dual Attached EISA FDDI adaptor that is
>>cabled directly into a Gigaswitch and not an FDDI concentrator.  Shouldn't
>>this be ok?
>
>
>That's absolutely fine. 

Yep...made sure we went A-B and B-A.  Just wanted to make sure this wasn't
causing our crashes.  After pulling cards, we found that any time a memory
card was in MEM3, we'd get thousands of errors in ERRLOG.SYS.  Pull the card
from MEM3 and all worked fine.  We also swapped cards to verify that the cards
were good.  

Thanks for the info!

-Richard



