S. Sanjay Gopal wrote:
> 
> We have a problem with some of Dec Alphas running Unix 4.0x and I
> was hoping someone could shed some light on it. For sometime now we
> have been running several jobs via shell scripts and they have been
> running fine. All these are computationally intensive and usually
> last for a week or more. More recently a lot of these jobs have
> been crashing midway. On analyzing the dumped core file we observe
> errors such as
> 
>         memory fault
>         illegal instruction
> 
> when trying to enter a sub-routine. In the calling function the
> arguments to the sub-routine are OK but inside the sub-routine the
> arguments seem to be zeroed out.
> 
 sanjay
> 

hi, sanjay,
we experienced similar crashes, when our programs had memory leaks
(malloc(), but no free()). Do you see very big core files? This could be
a hint... If so, you should examine your limits (ulimit). Maybe you ran
out of a limited ressource and the system gave you a blow.

Rolf
