In article <6moq97$6er@sol.sun.csd.unb.ca>, Robert Ford <robert@grover.mta.ca> writes:
|>Hi,
|>
|>I have recently aquired a Microvax II and I have hit a stumbling block.
|>
|>The self tests appear to work correctly.  At the >>> prompt, I can type
|>'show qbus' and I see the line:
|>
|>-20001468 (772150) = 0000 (154) RQDX3/KDA50/RRD50/RQC25/KFQSA-DISK
|><along with others>
|>

If you can do SHOW DEV and SHOW QBUS you probably have a uVAX III variant
rather than the (slower) uVAX II. (uVAX II says KA630 when it powers up, 
the others are KA640 or KA650 or KA655).

>When I try 'show dev', I get:
|>
|>UQSSP Disk Controller 0 (772150)  ; waits a long time before the next line
|>- ?

It can see the controller but it cannot find any drives through the controller.


|>I do have a TK70 controller card but have it removed temporarily.  Pulling the
|>drive controller and putting the tape controller gives the same type of
|>response.

I'm assuming that when you pull cards you are also verifying that the
vector and CSR settings of *all* the remaining cards are set properly?

If you are then you might have a grant problem or a controller problem.
The KDA50 disk controller can be a bit of a fiddle, the RQDX3 disk controller
has a tendency for the drive cables to come slightly free (at least mine do!)
but the TQK50/70 controllers should just work (assuming yours isn't bust).

So start by assuming a grant problem (especially if you have a BA23 or
a BA123 where the grant snakes along after the first 3 or 4 slots).

Post a list of what you have in your system and a diagram of which slot
each occupies. (And which box you have - or a description if you don't know).

The output from SHOW QBUS which just the CPU, memory and disk controller
would be useful.

Antonio

