The original DIGITAL logo, the one with the square dot's over the eye's
was in fact letters carved out of blocks of wood. Thus, the astute would
have noticed that the two i's in DIGITAL were unique.

As they were carved out of wood, it was appropriate for the background
colour to show though the blocks, thus if the background was black, the
letters were black and if the back ground were blue, the letters were
blue.

The enhancement of the logo in the early 90's was to foster a campaign of
brand recognition, and to do so meant to encourge the use of DIGITAL to a
greater extent by all staff than had been the case in the past. In the
past, using the logo meant having to have a graphic, whereas with the
newly revised logo, a specific electronic type and colour could be easily
used to represent the logo.

rtt



