Chris King (chris@csking.demon.co.uk) wrote:
: Richard Tomkins <neuron@cyberus.ca> writes
: >Let's see, well, OpenVMS can read and write NTFS. It's currently running
: >on some systems at DIGITAL. I had thought it was commercialy available,
: >but if you seem to get no-where finding out about it, then it's probably
: >just available to us.

: If you're talking about OpenVMS Disk Services for WindowsNT, this is a
: shipping product.

If he really was talking about NTDS, then the above statement "VMS can
read and write NTFS") is not quite correct.

From VMS' point of view, the served file system is a container file.
I heard about a utility to read from and write to it, but haven't seen
it yet. Besides that, it's not supported by DEC/Compaq (AFAIK, because
of the lack of documentation about NTFS).

Apart from that, NTDS is a fine product. A client on the NT system lets
the served space look like a local disk. One license is included in the
EIS package that replaced the NAS license shipped with VMS systems.

cu,
