in the bathroom cabinet, in containers that are cryptically labeled, often
with names that differ only in the case of the letters. The shroud is off
the lawnmower, because it's what you use to trim the hedges. The table saw
in the garage has all handshields and interlocks removed, because they are
just for newbies, and they get in the way of real work. 

  Now, you might want to live in such a house, since it's safe enough for
someone who "knows what they are doing", but, I'll take VMS, which has
plenty of dangerously powerful tools handy, but not where the unwashed can
get to them, and that are not invoked without some knowledge and
forethought. Sure, it may take a few seconds more, or a few keystrokes
more, but, it's worth it... 

(I'll leave it to a unix fan to do an unflattering description of what
a VMS house would be like...)

