For sale: Prioris XL, Celebris XL, and Prioris HX PowerGrade kits

Ever want to upgrade your Prioris or Celebris computer system?  Did
you find DEC's prices too high?

DEC was clearing out a warehouse, turning hardware into cash to make
their books look better at time of merger.  We bought a warehouse
full, including a bunch of PowerGrade kits to upgrade Prioris and
Celebris computers.  Here is the list without asking prices.  See my
earlier FS: PowerGrade posting for prices before I had a chance to
inventory exactly what is in the kits.  I may decide to adjust some of
the prices.  If so, will post again with prices.  I am open to all
reasonable offers for any individual item(s) or the whole collection.

"MLB" is DEC's abbreviation for Main Logic Board, what most of us
usually call a motherboard. 

I have included the list of parts available in the kits for all but
two marketing identifiers.  Note also that I have some spare MLB's and
other parts, so if your system requires a new MLB, I can add one to a
PowerGrade kit for a nomimal amount.  Older DECpc XL systems, either
486 or Socket 4 Pentium, require a new MLB.  I also have a limited
quantity of 166MHz Pentium processors, so when I run out of 166MHz
kits, I can upgrade a Pentium 133 kit for a nominal charge.

I have not tested out the Alpha PowerGrade kit yet.

