He said A-SMP, as in Asymmetric multiprocessing, I'd agree that it's a
confusing way to put it, and I'd agree that it would be much harder to
produce such a machine and manage it, you'd need different object
code, libraries etc for each processor type, and you couldn't have
threads moving from one processor to another without a lot of messing
around. Distributed processing using something like PVM across a
network is similar to ASMP, without the shared memory.

