What do you mean by hand tune ?
You should not in general have been altering SYSGEN parameters willy nilly.
Even in 1987 you should have been using AUTOGEN.
I am not sure the exact date when running Autogen with feedback came in that
may have been after 1987. 
With this mechanism you get the system to tune itself according to what has
been happening on the running system. 

As to hating DCL and thinking that the UNIX API is cleaner - you are the first
person who claims to have moved from VMS to Unix who I have ever come across
with this opinion.
