>
>

Most of what you like in WNT is a direct pinch from VMS with the names 
changed to protect the innocent/guilty.

You have had SYS$SYNCH in VMS since god knows when probably version 1.0.

Unfortunately the implementation of the API has been compromised in order to
accommodate backwards compatibility with Windows 3.11.
In particular there is no consistent returning of success/error status codes
from calls. Also string variables are passed as null terminated strings leading
to buffer overflow problems.
Also whereas with VMS a single function is heavily overloaded with similar 
tasks by passing different variables with Windows NT you have myriads of 
separate functions. This makes finding the required function extremely
time consuming in WNT.

