>   ("fatal drive error" after INIT).

At least in the case of the Fujitsu, I ran into an incompatibility with a PC
SCSI controller (the BusTech BT445C) that may be the same as what's biting
you with the 3100: Apparently, there's some timing in the SCSI spec that's
open to interpretation. The BusTech expected there to be some time delay
between having a signal asserted and the resulting acknowledgement; the
Fujitsu's Cirrus Logic SCSI interface didn't have any delay there. Result:
lots of errors. This seems like a possibility, anyway.



