>Can anyone direct me to some place to get docs on FILES-11 and BRU?  I
>would certainly appreciate any help here.

The official documents, of course, are in the RSX-11M manuals, but they
don't go into much technical details about the nitty-gritty layout.  For
these details, you almost need a RSX-11M source kit.

Of course, you don't have to go to such trouble if you have a RSX-11M
system or a VMS system with the VAX/RSX migration package (and thus
BRU) or BRUREAD (a DECUS utility, now available by anonymous FTP
from

ftp://sunsite.unc.edu/pub/academic/computer-science/history/pdp-11/rsx/bruread/

If the RSX or VMS system is on a network, it's then very easy
to move the files to wherever you want to use them.

If you don't have a running RSX or VMS system, I strongly advise that
you find someone who does with the appropriate peripherals to read your
tape(s).  It's literally a ten-minute job with the correct tools (which
I, and I'm sure many others, have.)

