IMHO shared-nothing is not the way to go, but u$oft apparently has a
religious opposition to shared-everything.

Consider the two approaches. 

Assume a shared-nothing environment wherein one runs eight copies of 4-CPU
DogPack (MCSC) on a hard-partitioned 32-CPU Wildfire. (I assume this will
be the u$oft approach).

Assume a shared-everything environment wherein one runs n instances of NT
on an APMP soft-partitioned 32-CPU Wildfire.

Methinks Option B would provide significantly greater scalability and
flexibility.

