> 
>    We are still looking for a 3.5" scsi drive (1 GB or greater) that
>    is known to work with the model 3100/30. In the meantime, attempts
>    to attach a 1 GB Fujitsu model M1606SAU have met with similar failure
>    ("fatal drive error" after INIT). If we succeed with some specific
>    model I will post to the group.

If you are using 5.5-2, the "fatal drive error" is quite likely to be
caused by the mode sense bits.  Wolfgang Moeller (I think he is at
moeller@gwdg.de) has posted some patches for VMS 5.5-2 which, among
things, cause it to accept these settings.  Alternately, it may be
possible to reprogram the mode sense bits on the drive.

We have had a 1GB Fujitsu working with a 3100/30, but I don't know the
drive's model number.

As for an RZ26, go for it.  The SCSI controller in a 3100/38 is
identical to a 3100/30.  In fact, VMS can't tell the two CPUs apart.
 
Good luck!

