Hi Boris,

Digital UNIX clustering is a shared everything (for the production
server version). Storage can be accessed by all the members in the
cluster using Distributed Raw Devices (and coming soon to a cluster near
you - Cluster File System for cluster wide file systems). With some
programming you can share even memory (using the Memory Channel API) -
By the way the MPI uses Memory Channel as its base messaging...
The biggest draw back of the shared nothing is: How to do implement 
Paralell Databases like OPS, it's not a problem on a TruCluster as we
we have simultanoues disk access and a Distibuted Lock Manager.
Digital supplies NT customers something called OSD (Operating System
Dependant) to allow the database I/O from all the members to the shared
disks.

The Oracle ( http://ntsolutions.oracle.com ) and Compaq's (
 http://www.windows.digital.com/clusters ) is a good place to start
looking...

