>    command have resulted in a "fatal drive error" message. We have
>    more or less ruled out problems due to improper termination and
>    jumper settings.
> 
>    My question is this: Should we assume that this particular model
>    drive is inherently imcompatible with a VAXstn 3100/30 ? If so,
>    can anyone recommend another brand/model of about that capacity
>    that is known to work with a VAXstn 3100/30 ?
> 
