Hi there - It just so happens I have a manual for one of those lurking
on my shelf..

the lights are numbered 0 - 7 from the RIGHT

0-3 are specific errors, whilst 4-7 are general components...

There is no match for the sequence in the book, but here's the 4-7
lights (x=on)

ooox = Time of year and non-volatile memory

ooxo = Low cost graphics

ooxx = Serial controller

oxoo = Cache

oxox = System memory boards

xooo = Network interface

xoxo = SCSI devices

xoxx = Audio

I guess this means you have one of a few combinations that could be
made up from the above. (Or the lights are broken <grin>)


