> I am using DEC C++ compiler and I need to increase the stack size. How can I
> do this?

I think that you need to change the stack size in the UNIX shell that you
are running (sh, csh, tcsh, etc). The command to type depends on what shell
you're using.  In csh, it's 'limit stacksize nnn' or 'limit stacksize
unlimited'. The "limit" command will tell you what the current limit is.

You might also find that the shell addresspace limit needs to be increased.

Also, the system parameters max-per-proc-stack-size, max-proc-address-space,
and vm-maxvas might all need adjustments depending on how much stack space
they need.

Hope it helps.

-Jeff

