>   too slow to see the technological discontinuity offered by RISC
>   and then indecisively floundered around for too long afterwards.
> 

BINGO!!!!   In the late 80's, many of the smarter powers at DEC (me excluded)
understood that RISC had a better long term viability than the VAX. In fact, 
Dave Cutler was driving that effort; however, nobody wanted to kill the goose that laid 
the golden eggs.  Each VAX sale had a high profit margin, and DEC built 
a cost structure to mirror this. 

RISC was a low profit margin business, and DEC needed to restructure 
the entire company.   Our president at Convex was the first to boast about 
this as the likely problem.  Well, Convex is now HP but his point is still 
well taken.  This is especially true since Convex's management was transplanted
from Mostek (with the exception of Bob Palmer who went somewhere else) ;-). 

I work for NORTEL now, and I am seeing the same major technological transition 
from circuit based to packet switched technologies.  Oh well, the only thing 
that is constant is change!!!!



