    no more sales planned - clearly misleading information since the sale
    of the entire company was by that time in the works.)

2   Digital management never released a key piece of financial information
    - that they were bleeding rivers at the FAB facility (this information
    only saw the light of day as a result of the settlement with Intel).

These two actions were more than just reprehensible, they appear to have
been a mechanism by which management artificially inflated Digital stock
prices, which I imagine should be grounds for SEC action and/or a
stockholder lawsuit (although against whom I cannot say, since the company 
is no more - maybe against the board and management?)

I cannot speak for other investors, but I certainly would have sold my
stock long before I did had I known of either Digital management's real
long term strategy or the magnitude of the FAB losses.

