>about finding monitors that work. The manual of the
>ZLXp-E2 lists 15 settings that require certain monitors,
>settable by a switch on the back of the card. 

there is a chart in one of the two manuals you got with this card (if you got a 
manual:). there are 4 DIP switches setable from the back of the card. setting 
them with all of them "down" (set towards the card), is something like 
1600X1200, at some high resolution. set them with the first and last switches 
"up" (away from the card). this will give you something that even low end 
multisync monitors can use. look thru the chart for the size screen and refresh 
rate, and compare it to the monitor you want to use. find one that is within 
the refresh range your monitor uses, at an acceptable size.

good luck.

