VMS clusters are indeed much more sophisticated, but the rest isn't
true:

Around 1986, when Compaq delivered the first 386 PC's, Novell NetWare
was still a 16-bit operating system (V2.0a), but it was capable of
saturating an Ethernet while talking to just two or three client PC's.
(With the server os running on a 6MHz '84 vintage IBM AT!)

