A few details would have been in order.  The following works fine
on our system (Multinet, maybe you have to change the smtp% part for other 
TCP/IP transports):

 $ subject = "this is a test"
 $ file    = somefile.txt
 $ address = "fred@nowhere.notreal.com"
 $ mail/subject="''subject'" 'file' smtp%"""''address'"""

Put this code snippet into your DCL procedure, and you should be all set.

