Hi Terry.

I'm not sure why nobody is pointing out the fact that the data bus of
the 21164 is 128 bits.  At the system level, the interface to the DIMM
may be through a 256 bit bus.  This facilitates the memory transactions,
which are always done one cache line at a time (512 bits) instead of by
bytes, words, longwords, or quadwords.

--Russell (speaking only for myself)

