   [crossposted to comp.sys.dec hoping for VAX advice]

    Hi,
    Both programs minicom and seyon provide dumb terminal access
through VT100/ANSI terminal emulation.  Both are probably included
with your distribution, but if not just check sunsite.unc.edu and
download whichever you want.

    You should attach the serial port to both the VAX and Linux boxen
using a null modem cable (pins 2 and 3 reversed), and then make
certain both the VAX and Linux side are configured to the same baud
rate, and commmunications options.  Depending on what's running on the
VAX (You didn't specify whether the VAX is running Ultrix or VMS) it
may want 7 bits, even parity, or 8 bits no parity.  (I don't have much
VMS or Ultrix experience, so I may be wrong here - anyone, please
chime up if you know more).  Either way, they both must match on each
side.

     You should also consider finding yourself a Q-BUS Ethernet
adapter for the MicroVAX.  They're pretty cheap these days, why not
see if anyone on comp.sys.dec is in the market to sell what you need?
Ethernet would be far more preferable over a dumb serial connection to
the VAX.

Good Luck!
J. Maynard Gelinas
UNIX System Administrator
maynard@jmnospamg.com

