We have just completed a migration of our EDI operations from VAX based
hardware to Alpha based hardware.  We relicensed DEC/EDI last summer in
aticipation of this activity.  Included in this relicense purchase was
support for all required software, including Object Broker.  At that
time, however, DEC no longer owned the rights to license Object Broker.
DEC had sold the Object Broker rights to BEA Systems, Inc of Sunnyvale,
CA.  In order to fulfill the Boeing purchase of DEC/EDI 2.1, which
required Object Broker, DEC shipped a copy of BEA Object Broker, version
3.0.

We decided not to install the BEA version of Object Broker on the Alpha
based machine.  The DEC version currently running on the VAX (v2.10 -
the final version sold or supported by DEC) was Alpha capable.  BEA
Object Broker 3.0 (the first version sold and supported by BEA) had not
been tested by us. This testing was deferred, pending completion of the
migration to the Alpha based machine.

DEC has recommended that we upgrade to v3.0 of Object Broker as soon as
possible because, among other reasons, all Object Broker support people
once employed by DEC are now employed by BEA.

BEA on the other hand has no record of a purchase of BEA Object Broker
by us, much less a support contract

Has anyone else had an experience like this? What was the outcome? What
sources of online support can I go to?

(FYI: BEA = BEA Systems, Inc. web site : http://www.beasys.com)

Thanks!

LMc




