JF Mezei <jfmezei.spamnot@videotron.ca> writes:

> Why would anyone think that a further delay of a non-existent chip
> cause Alpha to suddently take off ?

Intel has been relatively cheap, compared to alternatives (except for
their high-end stuff, but that's also a tiny niche).  Both cheap, fast
alphas, as well as the AMD compatible bus, could give alpha the same 
advantage, while Intels new offerings, like Xeon, and Merced if and when 
it appears, are scheduled to cost an arm and a leg, paid through the
nose. 

Everybody, including Intel and MS have been touting 64bitness, and with
pavlovian surety made the tie-adorned ranks drool.  Now, all of a
sudden, the 64bit market seems less diverse...

Compaq *could* choose to push Alpha harder, and probably use AMD in the
same motherboards.  SGI and Intergraph might settle for Alphas.  Things
might change.

~kzm
