I have a VAX 6000 system with 3 network interfaces (2 BNA's, 1 MNA). 
These feed various net segments. Each segment has 1 Infoserver 150 with
some extra disk space, and varying numbers of VXT2000 Xterminals, a
total of 40 over the three segments.  The terminals are running text
applications in each window, no graphics.

I need to re-arrange the nets and possibly consolidate some equipment
and so have some questions.  

1: Is there a practical limit to the number of Xterms a single
Infoserver can host ?

2. Is it a 'fixable' limit, addressable by adding more swap space or
memory, etc ?

3. Will I take a big performance hit if I put all 40 Xterms and three
Infoservers on the same physical network ??

Thanks fro any and all constructive inputs..

Bob Lombard



