Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec




We have a number of "OSF1 V4.0 878 alpha" workstations.  The following
simple Fortran90 code works on various other platforms but gives a
segmentation fault on our DEC boxes.  It may be that the large temporary
arrays created by the subroutine are being allocated on the stack
rather than the heap.  If so, can this behaviour be changed or
otherwise remedied?

----test.f90------

program test
  use foomod
  real, allocatable :: d(:,:)
  allocate( d(600,500) )
  d=3.14
  call foo( d )
  deallocate( d )
end program test

----foomod.f90----

module foomod
contains
  subroutine foo( d )
    real :: d(:,:)
    real :: tmp(size(d,1),size(d,2))
    tmp = cshift( cshift(d,1,dim=2) ,1,dim=1)  ! segmentation fault
  end subroutine foo
end module foomod

-----------------

compiled with 'f90 foomod.f90 test.f90'


Thanks for any help you can offer.

Darran.

