rubber@bounce.com (Keith Refson - real email address in signature) writes:

> I can't see any way this could be a bug in the code. Obviously I
> have checked for array bounds problems, uninitialized variables and
> found nothing.  More mysteriously exactly the same behaviour is
> observed when the code is compiled with f90 instead of f77.

From your symptoms, there is a 99.99% chance, that you have forgotten
to SAVE local variables that are supposed to keep their values across
invocations of a procedure.

Legacy code is typically full of such problems, because many Fortran
compilers used to SAVE by default and programmers forgot to SAVE.
